# True or myth? Five things everyone has heard
subtitle: "Five things almost everyone has heard, from goldfish memory to radioactive bananas: true or myth? Guess each, then find out why."
tags: biology, physics, health
format: quiz

## True or myth? Five things everyone has heard
feedback:
    style: warm
    perfect: Nobody fools you.
    good: A sharp eye for a myth.
    poor: These myths fool almost everyone.
    none: The myths won this round.
sources:
    - id: esb
      title: 'Lightning facts: the Empire State Building'
      authors: US National Weather Service
      year: 2023
      finding: the Empire State Building is struck about 25 times a year
    - id: bed
      title: Banana equivalent dose
      authors: Wikipedia
      year: 2025
      url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana_equivalent_dose
      finding: a banana's potassium-40 gives about 15 becquerels; the body keeps its potassium level constant

    icon gw size 340 set twemoji x 500 y 450 icon_look picture of brick hidden true
    text gw_l "Great Wall from space" x 500 y 215 font_size 48 hidden true
    icon fish size 340 set twemoji x 500 y 450 icon_look picture of fish hidden true
    text fish_l "3-second memory" x 500 y 215 font_size 48 hidden true
    icon bolt cites ["esb"] size 340 set twemoji x 500 y 450 icon_look picture of "cloud with lightning" hidden true
    text bolt_l "Never twice" x 500 y 215 font_size 48 hidden true
    icon banana cites ["bed"] size 340 set twemoji x 500 y 450 icon_look picture of banana hidden true
    text banana_l "Radioactive?" x 500 y 215 font_size 48 hidden true
    icon octo size 340 set twemoji x 500 y 450 icon_look picture of octopus hidden true
    text octo_l "Three hearts?" x 500 y 215 font_size 48 hidden true

    card title "True or myth?"

Five things almost everyone has heard. For each one: true, or myth?
    icon r_gw size 130 set twemoji x 180 y 400 icon_look picture of brick
    icon r_fish size 130 set twemoji x 340 y 400 icon_look picture of fish
    icon r_bolt size 130 set twemoji x 500 y 400 icon_look picture of "cloud with lightning"
    icon r_banana size 130 set twemoji x 660 y 400 icon_look picture of banana
    icon r_octo size 130 set twemoji x 820 y 400 icon_look picture of octopus
    parallel true

    hide r_gw r_fish r_bolt r_banana r_octo

First: you can see the Great Wall of China from space.
    draw gw gw_l

    quiz "The Great Wall can be seen from space with the naked eye. True or myth?"
        right: Myth. The wall is long but only about as wide as a road, and China's first astronaut, Yang Liwei, could not see it in 2003.
        * True
        + Myth

    text gw_v "MYTH" #b5482e x 790 y 560 font_size 60

    pause 1.5

    hide gw gw_l gw_v

Next, the goldfish, said to forget everything in three seconds.
    draw fish fish_l

    quiz "A goldfish's memory lasts only about three seconds. True or myth?"
        right: Myth. Goldfish remember for months: they learn when food comes, and which sound means dinner.
        * True
        + Myth

    text fish_v "MYTH" #b5482e x 790 y 560 font_size 60

    pause 1.5

    hide fish fish_l fish_v

Then the old saying that lightning never strikes the same place twice.
    draw bolt bolt_l

    quiz "Lightning never strikes the same place twice. True or myth?"
        right: Myth. Tall things get hit again and again: the Empire State Building is struck about twenty-five times a year.
        * True
        + Myth

    text bolt_v "MYTH" #b5482e x 790 y 560 font_size 60

    pause 1.5

    hide bolt bolt_l bolt_v

Now the breakfast table: bananas are said to be radioactive.
    draw banana banana_l

    quiz "Bananas are radioactive. True or myth?"
        right: True. A tiny share of their potassium is radioactive potassium-40, though your body keeps its potassium level steady, so it does no harm.
        + True
        * Myth

    text banana_v "TRUE" #2f6b8f x 790 y 560 font_size 60

    pause 1.5

    hide banana banana_l banana_v

And last, the octopus, said to have three hearts.
    draw octo octo_l

    quiz "An octopus has three hearts. True or myth?"
        right: True. Two hearts pump blood through the gills, and a third sends it round the body.
        + True
        * Myth

    text octo_v "TRUE" #2f6b8f x 790 y 560 font_size 60

    pause 1.5

    hide octo octo_l octo_v

You got {score} of {score_total}.
    draw r_gw r_fish r_bolt r_banana r_octo parallel true

And the two that sounded silliest were true.
    highlight r_banana r_octo effect circle
